WEBVTT

00:12.804 --> 00:15.682
The sun is so bright,
I can't open my eyes.

00:16.516 --> 00:18.852
When the humid air blows,

00:19.477 --> 00:21.479
it's hard to even breathe.

00:23.314 --> 00:26.359
It's already November,
but today it feels as hot as midsummer.

00:28.194 --> 00:30.530
This unexpected heatwave

00:30.613 --> 00:33.658
is throwing off all of my senses.

00:36.202 --> 00:40.248
A season that I thought had already passed
has come back.

00:43.042 --> 00:44.169
You've changed.

00:45.545 --> 00:46.504
How?

00:48.047 --> 00:48.923
You look old.

00:52.343 --> 00:53.261
Oh?

00:53.344 --> 00:54.304
Rin?

00:56.681 --> 00:57.599
Who's that?

01:00.643 --> 01:02.103
Nice to meet you.

01:02.187 --> 01:05.440
Mr. Hase and I were working together
with the catering.

01:05.523 --> 01:07.358
My name is Miyauchi Masumi.

01:19.496 --> 01:20.955
Why didn't you tell me?

01:21.664 --> 01:22.832
Well…

01:23.500 --> 01:24.709
Were you hiding it?

01:25.335 --> 01:29.130
Of course not.
It wasn't important enough to bring up.

01:31.883 --> 01:35.428
Why wouldn't you turn down
a job offer from your ex-girlfriend?

01:35.512 --> 01:39.682
Like I said, it wasn't like that.
It was a coincidence.

01:41.935 --> 01:43.895
There's nothing to worry about.

01:44.562 --> 01:48.149
Masumi and I… I mean…

01:48.233 --> 01:51.861
Ms. Miyauchi and I aren't the type
to hold onto feelings like that.

01:57.617 --> 02:00.370
This is unbelievable.

02:00.453 --> 02:01.329
What did you say?

02:05.458 --> 02:07.544
I just can't believe it.

02:07.627 --> 02:10.130
To me, it goes against common sense.

02:11.172 --> 02:14.134
And I think all my friends in Korea
would agree with me.

02:17.595 --> 02:19.556
Can we stop talking about that?

02:22.392 --> 02:24.185
You know it, don't you?

02:24.269 --> 02:26.980
Even if we argue over
what we think is common sense,

02:27.689 --> 02:29.899
it won't solve anything.

02:35.864 --> 02:37.073
Rin.

02:38.032 --> 02:40.368
I didn't tell you about Ms. Miyauchi,

02:41.327 --> 02:42.287
and I'm sorry.

02:44.664 --> 02:45.623
But

02:46.833 --> 02:50.295
the catering job gave me
a real sense of accomplishment.

02:52.547 --> 02:54.215
They might even introduce me to--

02:54.299 --> 02:56.342
I want to support your job.

02:56.426 --> 02:57.260
But…

02:59.637 --> 03:03.016
where is your courtesy as my boyfriend?

03:07.562 --> 03:11.941
Not to mention, an "ex-girlfriend"
is someone you fell in love with once.

03:12.025 --> 03:13.735
You can always fall in love again.

03:13.818 --> 03:15.445
- That will never happen.
- Why?

03:15.528 --> 03:16.821
Because I have you.

03:29.208 --> 03:31.127
I was able to become serious about cooking

03:32.587 --> 03:35.215
and was motivated
to take on the challenge of catering,

03:36.382 --> 03:38.593
all because of you.

03:43.139 --> 03:46.100
Just as you are working hard at animation,

03:46.184 --> 03:47.435
right now,

03:48.519 --> 03:51.022
I want to give my very best to my cooking.

03:56.361 --> 03:57.403
Okay.

03:58.696 --> 04:01.115
But I want to lay down some rules.

04:02.492 --> 04:05.328
I don't want you two to meet up alone.

04:05.954 --> 04:08.539
And I don't want you to contact her
if it's not about work.

04:13.169 --> 04:14.420
I promise.

04:15.004 --> 04:18.591
I will never do anything
that you wouldn't want me to do.

04:29.477 --> 04:30.603
Thank you.

04:37.277 --> 04:41.572
I know that asking him to turn down a job
for my sake is unreasonable.

04:44.659 --> 04:46.035
I understand that in my head,

04:46.619 --> 04:48.997
but not in my heart.

04:50.832 --> 04:51.958
Sorry for the wait.

04:53.626 --> 04:56.462
- Here.
- Thanks.

04:58.256 --> 05:00.717
They also had this.

05:02.260 --> 05:04.929
Oh, wow! I can't wait.

05:05.513 --> 05:06.347
Me too.

05:12.395 --> 05:14.939
I think I should talk to him about it,
after all.

05:15.523 --> 05:17.275
I'm sure Taiga will understand.

05:21.154 --> 05:22.071
Are you okay?

05:22.155 --> 05:23.573
I stepped on something.

05:25.074 --> 05:26.200
Let me take a look.

05:29.996 --> 05:32.040
It doesn't look like you're hurt anywhere.

05:33.833 --> 05:35.001
Park Rin.

05:36.169 --> 05:39.422
What if you ruin the mood by complaining?

05:40.465 --> 05:41.507
That's right.

05:41.591 --> 05:45.261
Sometimes you need to suck it up
and compromise a little.

05:46.888 --> 05:49.390
Let's make this a fun trip.

05:50.975 --> 05:52.101
- Let's.
- All right.

07:08.386 --> 07:10.012
It looks like a miniature town.

07:20.148 --> 07:23.401
Taiga? Are you afraid of heights?

07:24.777 --> 07:26.112
Not really.

07:27.905 --> 07:29.365
You're scared, aren't you?

07:29.866 --> 07:31.200
I'm not scared.

07:45.256 --> 07:46.674
That's what I'm talking about.

07:46.757 --> 07:48.676
I guess you haven't changed in that sense.

07:48.759 --> 07:51.053
Oh please. We're the same.

08:00.605 --> 08:02.315
Thanks for waiting.

08:07.570 --> 08:10.281
It's from Shige. Sorry, can I take this?

08:13.534 --> 08:15.203
Hello.

08:16.037 --> 08:18.956
Yes. It's hot today, isn't it?

08:24.754 --> 08:25.796
This is good.

08:26.631 --> 08:28.174
It goes well with this view.

08:31.093 --> 08:34.680
Thank you for bringing me to such
a beautiful place.

08:37.850 --> 08:42.313
I'm happy to be able to come here
with you.

08:44.649 --> 08:45.900
Me too.

08:46.609 --> 08:48.528
I'm glad I got to come here with you.

09:18.849 --> 09:19.725
Amazing…

09:19.809 --> 09:20.643
‪WEEKLY SQUAT

09:47.878 --> 09:49.880
A lot of people
get the wrong idea about it,

09:49.964 --> 09:52.174
so I'm glad you showed interest.

09:52.258 --> 09:53.342
Oh, it's nothing.

09:53.426 --> 09:55.761
- If I hear of anything, I'll let you know.
- Thank you.

09:55.845 --> 09:57.722
You'd better be grateful.

09:57.805 --> 09:58.639
Thank you!

10:03.686 --> 10:04.979
I'll get going then.

10:05.062 --> 10:06.814
- Okay.
- See you.

10:07.523 --> 10:08.524
Thank you!

10:11.694 --> 10:13.988
I had no luck
with three machines in a row,

10:14.071 --> 10:16.073
but I'm finally getting back on track.

10:16.824 --> 10:19.160
Before I forget… I got your favorite.

10:19.827 --> 10:22.330
- Strawberry chocolate.
- Thanks.

10:22.997 --> 10:26.083
Who were those people?
I've never seen them here before.

10:30.046 --> 10:33.716
They're basically… my business partners.

10:35.885 --> 10:36.719
What are you saying?

10:37.386 --> 10:41.182
I may not look it, but I'm actually
thinking about things, all right?

10:41.265 --> 10:43.017
Just trust me.

10:56.405 --> 10:57.865
This is a torii?

11:01.994 --> 11:04.538
I WANT TO MEET MY SOULMATE

11:04.622 --> 11:06.707
You write your wish here, huh?

11:11.462 --> 11:13.631
Since we're here,
why don't you write something too?

11:15.341 --> 11:16.801
Maybe I will.

11:21.639 --> 11:23.516
I WANT MY EX-GIRLFRIEND BACK

11:23.599 --> 11:25.393
PLEASE REKINDLE OUR RELATIONSHIP

11:30.606 --> 11:31.440
Rin?

11:34.360 --> 11:36.946
We don't have time, so let's go.

11:55.589 --> 11:57.675
You don't seem to have energy.

11:58.217 --> 11:59.552
Are you not feeling well?

12:00.719 --> 12:03.722
Sorry… But I'm feeling just fine.

12:09.520 --> 12:10.855
It's Yung-yeol.

12:12.815 --> 12:14.191
Hello?

12:14.275 --> 12:16.777
Park Rin. Did you see my message?

12:18.112 --> 12:21.407
Oh, about your souvenir?
I'll check right now.

12:23.576 --> 12:25.077
What is this?

12:25.161 --> 12:28.956
Local sake from Izu and pickled wasabi?

12:29.874 --> 12:33.335
Rin. Maybe you shouldn't
talk on the phone while on the bus.

12:36.130 --> 12:37.423
Sorry.

12:39.383 --> 12:41.385
Sorry. I'll call you back later.

13:24.762 --> 13:26.263
Thank you for waiting.

13:26.347 --> 13:29.141
Here's your creamy lemon pasta
with salmon and mushroom

13:29.767 --> 13:32.228
and roasted pork with beet sauce.

13:32.311 --> 13:34.647
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

13:35.648 --> 13:36.941
Enjoy.

13:39.068 --> 13:40.152
All right.

13:48.285 --> 13:49.286
What's wrong?

13:51.288 --> 13:54.333
I ordered roast beef,

13:55.000 --> 13:56.043
but this is…

13:57.461 --> 14:01.173
roasted pork with beet sauce.

14:07.888 --> 14:09.056
You're right…

14:12.434 --> 14:13.310
Excuse me.

14:14.436 --> 14:16.063
I'll eat that then.

14:17.731 --> 14:21.610
You were interested
in the creamy pasta too, so we can swap.

14:22.278 --> 14:23.279
This is…

14:24.738 --> 14:26.490
the restaurant's mistake, right?

14:28.075 --> 14:29.952
Yeah, it is, but…

14:30.035 --> 14:32.621
Since I work at Tanomi,

14:32.705 --> 14:35.332
I don't like making a fuss
in these situations.

14:36.917 --> 14:39.420
I know that everyone makes mistakes.

14:40.296 --> 14:42.673
But wouldn't it be better
to let them know?

14:45.551 --> 14:47.970
But I'll eat it, so isn't that fine?

14:56.687 --> 14:58.188
So basically,

14:59.690 --> 15:01.525
I'm in the wrong again, huh?

15:02.151 --> 15:03.152
I didn't say that--

15:03.235 --> 15:07.114
You said that we shouldn't
argue about our cultural differences,

15:07.197 --> 15:08.908
but if we don't acknowledge that,

15:09.491 --> 15:11.911
I'll look like a bad person
who does everything wrong.

15:19.919 --> 15:24.465
That makes me more sad.

16:20.771 --> 16:22.022
They don't have it.

16:42.126 --> 16:43.669
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

16:44.336 --> 16:46.296
Do you have ramune?

16:47.131 --> 16:48.966
I'm sorry, we don't have that.

16:53.387 --> 16:54.680
They don't have it…

17:13.532 --> 17:15.868
STUDIO JUPITET
YOUR APPLICATION IS COMPLETED

17:15.951 --> 17:17.870
THANK YOU FOR APPLYING TO OUR STUDIO

17:22.708 --> 17:24.960
The most important thing

17:25.044 --> 17:28.756
is to lead a stable life.

17:28.839 --> 17:31.759
Trust your mother, okay?

17:31.842 --> 17:33.969
- The art instructor position?
- Yes.

17:34.053 --> 17:36.805
You have no other options, right?

17:36.889 --> 17:37.890
STUDIO JUPITET

17:51.737 --> 17:53.155
The results aren't out yet…

18:01.413 --> 18:03.165
FOR JAPANESE-KOREAN COUPLES

18:03.248 --> 18:05.125
JAPANESE BOYFRIENDS AND KOREAN GIRLFRIENDS

18:05.209 --> 18:07.252
HOW TO MAKE UP FAST

18:14.259 --> 18:16.804
- Welcome back.
- Hey.

18:24.061 --> 18:25.020
Are you going to sleep already?

18:27.189 --> 18:28.524
I'm a little tired.

18:29.525 --> 18:33.028
Okay. It was a long day, after all.

18:35.864 --> 18:37.241
Good night.

18:37.825 --> 18:39.326
Good night.

19:17.990 --> 19:19.575
TANOMI

19:19.658 --> 19:21.618
What? Where's Mr. Hase today?

19:21.702 --> 19:25.080
Oh, he took today and tomorrow off.

19:26.707 --> 19:28.292
He's on a trip with his girlfriend.

19:28.375 --> 19:31.545
Oh, a trip? How nice.

19:31.628 --> 19:34.673
It's Rin's something-list.

19:35.174 --> 19:37.217
- Bucket list.
- Yeah, that.

19:37.301 --> 19:40.679
One of the items on her list of things
to do before she dies

19:40.762 --> 19:42.431
was to drink ramune at a hot spring.

19:42.514 --> 19:46.393
What? Mr. Hase is such a nice boyfriend!

19:48.812 --> 19:49.688
Here.

19:50.772 --> 19:54.610
Noa, do you have anything you want to do
before you die?

19:54.693 --> 19:55.527
‪What?

20:01.033 --> 20:02.659
I've never thought about it.

20:04.995 --> 20:07.873
I got a lot of good feedback on this.

20:08.457 --> 20:12.169
As soon as I posted it on our social media
I got reservations from foreigners.

20:12.252 --> 20:13.420
‪Oh!

20:14.338 --> 20:15.797
Really?

20:16.381 --> 20:18.842
If I update the menu, can I ask you again?

20:19.426 --> 20:22.971
Sure. It didn't take long anyway.

20:23.055 --> 20:24.056
Okay.

20:26.308 --> 20:28.602
A bucket list, huh?

20:28.685 --> 20:31.813
But I've already done everything
that I've wanted to do.

20:31.897 --> 20:33.649
As expected.

20:34.566 --> 20:35.692
I would rather

20:35.776 --> 20:39.780
list all the things that I regret,
and remove each one.

20:40.572 --> 20:43.659
Then what is your number one regret?

20:44.618 --> 20:46.203
I should've divorced earlier.

20:47.996 --> 20:49.498
I see.

20:50.582 --> 20:51.833
What about you?

20:51.917 --> 20:54.378
If you could go back in time just once,

20:54.461 --> 20:58.257
and remove just one regret off your list,
what would you do?

21:00.300 --> 21:02.844
Let's see…

21:06.640 --> 21:07.557
I think

21:08.558 --> 21:12.271
you should hurry up and move on
to the next chapter of your life.

21:17.734 --> 21:19.945
Taiga, what do you want to do?

21:21.280 --> 21:23.657
I can't make a decision that easily.

21:24.449 --> 21:27.327
I've dedicated
more than half of my life to track.

21:28.287 --> 21:31.248
But in the end, you'll spend most
of your life not doing track.

21:31.957 --> 21:35.752
You have to plan for your life
after graduation.

21:41.675 --> 21:43.385
You wouldn't understand, Masumi.

21:55.022 --> 21:58.734
I guess my biggest regret

21:59.651 --> 22:02.946
is that I hurt my ex-boyfriend.

22:04.448 --> 22:06.199
I contradicted myself.

22:07.200 --> 22:08.785
At first, I liked him

22:08.869 --> 22:12.456
because he was so unbelievably
determined to chase his dream.

22:13.790 --> 22:17.461
But in the end, I broke up with him
because "he wouldn't face reality."

22:20.213 --> 22:22.966
Do you still have feelings for him,

22:23.884 --> 22:28.013
or do you just feel regretful
that you couldn't be kind?

22:57.501 --> 22:59.044
TAIGA, HOW IS IT GOING?

22:59.127 --> 23:01.379
IF YOU'RE IN NUMAZU,
I RECOMMEND THIS SPOT.

23:04.174 --> 23:05.258
Excuse me.

23:07.010 --> 23:08.178
Go ahead.

23:42.921 --> 23:46.091
They're really… amazing.

23:47.717 --> 23:50.846
Their themes and motifs are all so unique.

23:50.929 --> 23:51.972
It's so entertaining.

23:53.306 --> 23:55.225
Is that right?

24:00.063 --> 24:01.439
That reminds me…

24:02.440 --> 24:06.069
If you had an infinite amount
of time and money,

24:06.653 --> 24:08.196
what would you like to create?

24:14.536 --> 24:18.957
What is the message
you want to convey through this piece?

24:23.461 --> 24:24.379
Rin?

24:27.632 --> 24:28.550
Are you okay?

24:32.345 --> 24:35.307
Sorry… I need to go to the bathroom.

24:55.785 --> 24:56.870
Thanks for waiting.

25:01.541 --> 25:02.417
Rin.

25:04.002 --> 25:04.961
Look at this.

25:10.634 --> 25:12.594
You haven't been smiling at all.

25:13.094 --> 25:14.179
Have you noticed?

25:20.393 --> 25:22.938
If this is how it's going to be
until the end of the trip

25:24.272 --> 25:25.899
we can't enjoy it.

25:30.987 --> 25:34.157
What are you thinking right now?

25:36.993 --> 25:38.787
Whatever it is, just tell me.

25:59.808 --> 26:00.767
What's wrong?

26:01.893 --> 26:03.144
TAIGA, HOW IS IT GOING?

26:03.228 --> 26:04.771
IF YOU'RE IN NUMAZU,
I RECOMMEND THIS SPOT.

26:04.854 --> 26:06.064
This is…

26:06.940 --> 26:08.942
not about work, is it?

26:11.319 --> 26:13.780
No, look at the rest of it.

26:15.115 --> 26:16.616
She's just researching things
for catering--

26:16.700 --> 26:19.953
It's impossible to differentiate
between what's work and what's not.

26:20.578 --> 26:22.080
Even if it's about work,

26:22.163 --> 26:24.749
why would she message you
while you're on vacation?

26:25.875 --> 26:28.545
I get it.
Let's go back to the inn for now.

26:32.382 --> 26:33.341
Rin.

26:34.968 --> 26:36.303
Taiga,

26:37.095 --> 26:40.807
you care more about what others think
than how I feel, even at a time like this.

26:40.890 --> 26:43.560
That's not true.

26:43.643 --> 26:47.439
More like, I thought we settled
the issue about Ms. Miyauchi.

26:47.522 --> 26:51.526
But when things like this happen,
I can't help but worry.

26:52.027 --> 26:53.528
Try to understand my feelings--

26:53.611 --> 26:55.572
Come on, already.

26:58.325 --> 27:02.495
Am I that untrustworthy to you?

27:05.874 --> 27:06.708
Well,

27:06.791 --> 27:08.585
try to have some trust in him.

27:10.920 --> 27:14.174
One day, Aki will find honest work.

27:16.468 --> 27:17.969
I wonder.

27:19.346 --> 27:22.140
Apparently, he is thinking about it,
but who knows…

27:24.184 --> 27:25.060
Oh?

27:25.143 --> 27:26.227
Hyeongnim!

27:27.103 --> 27:28.188
Dongsaeng!

27:29.689 --> 27:32.901
The bond between brothers
is incredible, isn't it?

27:33.401 --> 27:35.570
So, what were you talking about?

27:54.839 --> 27:55.840
Noa…

27:58.551 --> 28:01.054
felt that way about me, huh?

28:04.849 --> 28:07.811
I'm so pathetic.

28:08.603 --> 28:10.563
That's not true, Aki.

28:12.107 --> 28:13.066
But I…

28:15.026 --> 28:17.445
love Noa.

28:18.696 --> 28:20.657
The love I have for her in my heart

28:21.408 --> 28:23.910
is stronger than anybody else
and I know it.

28:25.703 --> 28:26.704
I understand.

28:28.331 --> 28:30.333
It's all about the heart.

28:31.626 --> 28:33.962
As long as you have love,
it will work out.

28:35.964 --> 28:38.758
I am on your side, until I die.

28:43.138 --> 28:44.389
Hyeongnim…

28:50.353 --> 28:51.229
Dongsaeng.

28:56.484 --> 28:58.236
Hyeongnim!

29:40.737 --> 29:41.613
Rin?

29:49.579 --> 29:53.458
UNFORTUNATELY, WE WILL NOT BE ACCEPTING
YOUR APPLICATION AT THIS TIME.

30:14.020 --> 30:17.649
You can try again.

30:22.278 --> 30:23.488
Again?

30:24.405 --> 30:25.448
When?

30:29.994 --> 30:32.789
This was my last chance

30:34.374 --> 30:36.125
to prove to eomma…

30:40.880 --> 30:43.842
Prove what to your mother?

30:51.724 --> 30:55.645
She has been telling me to work
as an instructor in Korea

30:56.187 --> 30:57.605
after I graduate.

30:59.899 --> 31:04.279
I thought that I could prove myself
to eomma if I got into a studio.

31:12.537 --> 31:14.581
Why didn't you tell me any of this?

31:16.958 --> 31:18.751
Because you…

31:19.752 --> 31:22.630
are moving forward, one step at a time.

31:23.548 --> 31:27.802
While I don't even know
what I want to create.

31:29.470 --> 31:31.180
I was too ashamed.

31:33.766 --> 31:35.476
It's nothing to be ashamed about.

31:38.938 --> 31:40.273
But Rin…

31:41.983 --> 31:45.820
You said it was to prove yourself
to your mother, right?

31:48.114 --> 31:49.490
I don't know,

31:50.074 --> 31:54.454
but I feel like
that shouldn't be your goal.

32:08.968 --> 32:12.013
What do you want to do?

32:19.604 --> 32:20.897
I don't know.

32:23.816 --> 32:26.277
I want to become an animator,

32:26.361 --> 32:28.404
but nothing is working out.

32:31.115 --> 32:34.577
But I don't want to give up
and go back to Korea either.

32:36.037 --> 32:39.207
I want to believe in my talent
and challenge myself.

32:41.209 --> 32:42.585
But nothing is working…

32:59.477 --> 33:03.022
Taiga, what about you?

33:05.191 --> 33:06.025
‪What?

33:09.070 --> 33:11.739
Where is our relationship headed?

33:25.753 --> 33:27.213
In the end…

33:30.842 --> 33:32.552
it's your choice.

33:39.142 --> 33:43.396
I want to respect your decision the most.

33:55.074 --> 33:56.826
You're fine with that, Taiga?

33:58.995 --> 33:59.829
‪What?

34:01.039 --> 34:02.582
Why are you like that?

34:04.250 --> 34:07.754
Just think about it.

34:08.504 --> 34:09.964
If, let's say,

34:11.507 --> 34:14.177
you decided to go back to Korea…

34:16.721 --> 34:18.473
I don't have any right to stop you.

34:19.432 --> 34:20.600
Isn't that right?

34:29.025 --> 34:30.443
Then how can you

34:33.154 --> 34:35.114
call yourself my boyfriend?

34:38.785 --> 34:40.119
What do you mean?

34:41.204 --> 34:42.955
Don't you understand?

34:43.539 --> 34:46.417
All I wanted was for you to say

34:46.501 --> 34:48.336
that I belonged here.

34:48.419 --> 34:50.338
That I could stay here.

34:56.344 --> 34:59.388
I wish you would've accepted me,
even just for a second.

35:03.226 --> 35:05.103
Why don't you get it?

35:13.778 --> 35:16.989
Sorry. I can't keep up with you.

35:18.950 --> 35:20.576
It's too difficult for me.

35:29.460 --> 35:30.503
I can't anymore…

35:32.922 --> 35:33.965
Let's break up.

37:28.079 --> 37:31.999
The reason we broke up
was not because of his ex-girlfriend,

37:33.960 --> 37:38.297
nor because of our upbringing,
personalities, or timing.

37:45.096 --> 37:48.432
In the end, our will wasn't strong enough.

37:49.350 --> 37:52.895
Our will to stay with each other
until the end, no matter what.

38:19.880 --> 38:22.049
If I had gone back to Taiga at that time…

38:24.468 --> 38:28.889
I wonder if things
would have been different for us?

38:33.477 --> 38:35.271
- Welcome.
- Good work.

38:35.896 --> 38:36.897
I like you.

38:36.981 --> 38:38.190
PREVIEW

38:38.941 --> 38:41.110
Don't come near her ever again.

38:41.193 --> 38:42.862
THIS DRAMA IS FICTION AND ALL CHARACTERS
AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTIONAL

38:42.945 --> 38:43.821
